-- _relation_quote_verified searches EVERY session's payloads with no structured ref_id in
-- the manifest, so a new REF-00971's quote could have verified against the old REF-00971's
-- bytes and read as correct.
--
-- THE RULE THIS ESTABLISHES: RETIRE THE IDENTIFIER, DELETE THE CONTENT. The owner ruled
-- these rows untrusted and they are gone -- no evidence_source, no extraction, no
-- determination survives. What is retained is the identifier and just enough to say what it
-- named. That is the reconciliation of two things that looked opposed: the corpus really is
-- cleared, and the identifiers really are spent. Keeping the full rows flagged-but-visible
-- would have preserved exactly what was ruled untrustworthy.
--
-- WHY source_locators AND NOT reference_stubs. Both carry status CHECK (... 'RETIRED') and
-- both are in dbcore.ref_id_homes, so either would hold the floor. reference_stubs was
-- merged INTO source_locators by migration 062 and has had no writer since; reviving a
-- retired table to solve a problem the live one already solves is how a schema grows a
-- second home (rule 5). And source_locators already carries this exact shape of record --
-- its recovered_from vocabulary includes 'retracted-2026-09-01-owner-ruling' from the
-- item-layer retraction.
--
-- THESE ROWS DO MORE THAN HOLD A FLOOR, which is why they carry the real identifiers rather
-- than being bare tombstones. db.py insert_evidence_source pre-checks an incoming DOI
-- against source_locators, so a re-run that re-admits one of these papers is refused and
-- pointed at its ORIGINAL ref_id -- R9 ("pre-check the DOI; cross-file the existing ref_id,
-- never duplicate") working as written. The identifier keeps meaning what it meant instead
-- of being reissued to something else or stranded.
--
-- NO url IS CARRIED, deliberately. The scheduled url-verification workflow claims rows with
-- a URL and a NULL verification_status and commits a DB blob straight to main (CLAUDE.md
-- rule 3 / R10). DOI, PMID and title identify these works without putting thirteen
-- tombstones into that pool.
